From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:23:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Bridge message ids, reactions and replies to the
 transport

The webOS IM transport shows reactions as badges on stored messages and
renders replies as quote cards, both keyed by the network message id
(serviceMessageId). It talks to protocol plugins through conversation
data and the webos-im-* signals, as the Telegram and WhatsApp plugins
do.

- Before writing a message, set "webos-msg-id" on the conversation so
  the transport stores the Discord message id with the row.
- For replies, set "webos-quoted-id/-from/-text", taken from
  referenced_message or, for gateway replies that only carry a
  message_reference, from a bounded cache of recently delivered
  messages.
- Emit "webos-im-outbox-id" when the echo of our own message arrives,
  so the outbox row gets its network id.
- Turn MESSAGE_REACTION_ADD/REMOVE into "webos-im-reaction" instead of
  the "reacted with" system message (and its REST fetch).
- Handle "webos-im-send-reaction" by PUT/DELETE on the reactions
  endpoint, finding the channel through a message id to channel map.
- Pass the "webos-reply-to" id that the transport sets on the
  conversation as the message_reference of the next message sent.

discord_react_cb is no longer called, so mark it G_GNUC_UNUSED.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 libdiscord.c | 319 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 276 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

